      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports telepractice speech-language therapy for people with aphasia, but it does not define “language therapy” as a general assessment-and-training intervention for language difficulties.",
        "The wording broadens the source beyond the packet’s scope by presenting aphasia as an example of a wider language-therapy definition rather than as the study population for Tele-SLT.",
        "The phrase “live, delayed, or mixed formats” is a paraphrase of synchronous, asynchronous, and combined formats, but the definition should not present that study-specific framing as the general sense of the term."
